Description: Boswas OS system applications
 The applications every Boswas OS desktop comes with, built on the Boswas
 Fluent toolkit so that they look and behave alike:
 .
  * Files: a file manager with tabs, search, the Trash, drives, undo, and
    copying in the background
  * Terminal: a terminal emulator with tabs and colour schemes
  * Text Editor: a plain text editor with tabs that keeps encodings and
    line endings
  * Calculator: standard, scientific and programmer modes, dates and unit
    converters
  * Task Manager: processes, performance, start-up applications, users
    and services
  * Photos: picture viewer, editor, gallery and slideshow
  * Media Player: music and video with a library, playlists and MPRIS
  * Camera: photos and video from a webcam
  * Document Viewer: a PDF reader
  * Archive Manager: ZIP and TAR archives (7z and RAR with 7zip)
  * Clock: alarms, timers, stopwatch and world clock
  * Calendar: a local calendar with reminders and iCalendar files
 .
 Each application is one program and runs as the desktop user. None of
 them starts a shell or keeps running in the background, except the small
 reminders service that rings alarms and shows calendar reminders.
